WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.700
This is the DP Pod Episode 85. I'm Dan Pere. He's Patrick Novak. Dan, I have to ask, did you actually look at your inverter app this morning? Or are you just going to pretend the sun showed up on schedule? I looked, and then I immediately started wondering what a whole country looks like when it does the same thing at once. That is a very you leap. India's the leap. They just posted their highest ever month of solar generation, October of 2026, and it actually moved the fossil share on the grid.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:33.540
Then, it is time for the positive papers, because that number is not a vibe.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.760
Clean energy trackers at CREA logged it as the biggest monthly solar total India has ever

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:44.000
put on a grid, utility scale farms and rooftops more than one state all stacking in the same

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:44.340
month.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.720
And the thing I care about is the mechanism.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.280
More cheap mid-day electrons, fewer fossil plants running in the middle of the day, households

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.620
and businesses see a lower marginal price when that share rises.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:56.440
Wait.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:56.580
Great.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.280
Highest month on record.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:00:59.360
Highest ever?

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.480
Exceeded every previous monthly total they have.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.940
That is a real grid, not a demo farm.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:05.820
It is.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:12.400
CREA logged parallel milestones in other countries the same week, so this is not a one-off press release.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.880
Here's where I get interested as an operator.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.200
I put solar on my own roof, so I already know the pretty part.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:19.580
Nune looks fantastic.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:24.260
The ugly part is the evening bank, when everybody lands at once and the sun has clocked off.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:28.980
You are describing the duck curve with airplanes, and I hate how well that works.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.140
Arrival banks are exactly that.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.480
You can handle a mid-day lull, you cannot fake 12 jets on the ramp with no tugs.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.920
Grid operators still have an open question.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.000
How do you cover those evening peaks without a pile of new storage?

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.520
I will steal Manure version because it is the stronger one.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:49.000
You are not saying the record is fake, you are saying a monthly generation trophy can

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.940
hide a daily shape problem, and until storage shows up, coal still covers supper.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.320
That is exactly it.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:59.860
Fair, and I will grant the shape problem. Evening still needs a plan.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:05.700
What I will not grant is treating the record as a rounding error. Capacity is being added,

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:11.060
rooftop programs are growing next to the big ground mounted arrays, and the fossil share for that

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.180
month did drop. I will meet you there. The drop is the part I would actually bet on,

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.420
because builders shipped metal, not slides.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.600
Where we still split is how far this pattern travels.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.420
I want to see the same monthly record in places

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.520
that do not have India's solar resource

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:26.820
before I call it a template.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.000
And I think the template is already the mix.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.580
Big arrays plus rooftops, not the latitude.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.140
We can watch the next country CREA posts

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:34.980
and settle it then.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:35.640
Deal.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.480
Speaking of things you can actually put in a person,

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.240
there is a thumb implant that works like a tiny hip.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.020
Go on.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:47.640
Advanced thumb arthritis, the base joint, the trapezium bone, instead of pulling that

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:52.780
bone out and leaving you with a grind, surgeons drop in a ball and socket implant that restores

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:53.380
the surface.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:56.700
Through the same kind of approach they already use for hips and shoulders.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:00.140
Same family of technique, which is the adoption story.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.180
Hand surgeons already know that hardware language.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:04.220
And the trials?

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:10.000
Patients got range of motion comparable to a healthy thumb, better grip, lower pain scores,

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.800
and they could do ordinary hand tasks that pain had taken away.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:15.300
Comparable to healthy.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.640
That is the claim from the early results.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.480
Okay, that is actually wild.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:23.060
Caveats, because I can hear myself overselling a joint.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.120
Advanced arthritis only.

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:27.180
Longer follow-up still missing.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:32.240
And insurers have not decided whether they will pay for an implant versus the old excision.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:34.840
See, that is the field failure I wait for.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.900
A beautiful implant that a benefits clerk will not code.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.780
If the established procedure is cheaper on paper, this sits on a shelf.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:42.540
True.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.600
The design still wins on mechanics.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.240
You keep a joint instead of deleting one, but mechanics do not build themselves.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:53.600
If I were a builder on that team, I would be walking insures through grip strength numbers

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:54.640
not renderings.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:55.740
Agreed.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.000
And while we are in the clinic, there is a blood pressure story that made me sit up.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.620
Hormone-driven hypertension.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:07.300
Roughly 10 to 15% of high blood pressure cases are pushed by too much aldosterone.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:13.140
A drug called Bactrostat blocks that production at the source instead of just chasing the number downstream.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.080
Hang on, 10 to 15% of all hypertension.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:19.420
Of the cases tied to that excess hormone, yes.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.260
That is not a rounding error, that is a waiting room.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:25.420
In the study, it reversed the hormone-driven high readings,

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:29.040
and the effect size beat typical blood pressure drugs in that subgroup.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.900
some people kept normal numbers for years after they stopped the course.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.640
Years after they stopped?

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.020
That is what the researchers documented.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:39.860
I almost called it a cure and then I heard myself.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:42.880
